# A REPLY as a server sends it (RFC 8415 section 18.3.2), reconstructed by hand: the server
# identifier, the client identifier, an IA_NA with T1 1500 s, T2 2400 s and one address,
# DNS servers (RFC 3646), a domain search list, an NTP Server option (RFC 5908) with one
# server address, and the Client FQDN of RFC 4704 with the S flag and a full name.
#
# msg-type REPLY, transaction id 0x1d2e3f
07 1d 2e 3f
# option 2, server identifier, 18 octets: DUID-UUID
00 02 00 12
00 04
00 11 22 33 44 55 46 77 88 99 aa bb cc dd ee ff
# option 1, client identifier, 14 octets: DUID-LLT, hardware type 1, time 0x2c3d4e5f, MAC
00 01 00 0e
00 01 00 01 2c 3d 4e 5f 00 00 5e 00 53 02
# option 3, IA_NA, 40 octets: IAID 0x5e005302, T1 1500, T2 2400
00 03 00 28
5e 00 53 02
00 00 05 dc
00 00 09 60
# option 5, IA Address, 24 octets: 2001:db8:1::100, preferred 3000 s, valid 4000 s
00 05 00 18
20 01 0d b8 00 01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 01 00
00 00 0b b8
00 00 0f a0
# option 23, DNS servers, 16 octets: 2001:db8::53
00 17 00 10
20 01 0d b8 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 53
# option 24, domain search list, 32 octets: "example.test." and "lab.example.test."
00 18 00 20
07 65 78 61 6d 70 6c 65 04 74 65 73 74 00
03 6c 61 62 07 65 78 61 6d 70 6c 65 04 74 65 73 74 00
# option 56, NTP server, 20 octets: NTP_SUBOPTION_SRV_ADDR (1), 16 octets, 2001:db8::123
00 38 00 14
00 01 00 10
20 01 0d b8 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 01 23
# option 39, client FQDN, 22 octets: flags S (0x01), the name "laptop.example.test."
00 27 00 16
01
06 6c 61 70 74 6f 70 07 65 78 61 6d 70 6c 65 04 74 65 73 74 00
